meta {
  name: Remove a skill (admin)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/skills/{{skillName}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Deletes the skill's folder from the workspace and forgets its configuration. Admin only —
  and specifically the `skills:delete` capability, which is in the DANGER tier, so reaching
  this from chat (`qj_api`) additionally needs a typed `confirm=true`.

  409 for a skill discovered under a personal `~/.claude/skills` or `~/.copilot/skills` — that
  belongs to the operator's own tooling, not to QuickJoiner. Disable it instead: PATCH
  /api/skills/{name} with `{"enabled": false}`, or `qj skills disable <name>`.

  Returns `{removed, configuration_forgotten}`. `configuration_forgotten: false` means the
  files are gone but the stored row survived, so reinstalling this name would inherit its old
  scope/enabled state.

  Stored secrets are NOT removed — a value such as OCTOPUS_API_KEY may serve other skills.
  Clear one explicitly via DELETE /api/skills/secrets/{key}.
}
